per tweet, though.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.400
-Oh, so you can't
vote yes and no.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.234
-That's -- That would be
counterintuitive.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:40.267
-Well, I'm just --
-Yeah, so you would -- yes.

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:41.868
You can vote on every one
if you like.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:45.667
-Is there any way to vote no
multiple times for one --

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:46.801
for the same tweet?

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.167
-No, that is --
You cannot do that, no.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.968
-No -- No multiple thumbs down.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.000
-No multiple thumbs down,
Tariq, no.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.167
Whatever you choose
is locked in for that tweet.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.501
-So then there'd be
no multiple thumbs up, either.

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:01.367
-Ah, see?
That's how they get you.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.100
-You guys should go out
after the show.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.200
